figure advanced permissions \\n\\nRunner Registration \\n\\n<::before><::after> New project runners can be registered \\n\\nExisting runners are not affected. To permit runner registration for all projects, enable this setting in the Admin area in Settings > CI/CD. \\n\\nSave changes  [ Cancel  ](/admin/projects/root/janusgraph)\\n\", url='http://the-agent-company.com:8929/admin/projects/root/janusgraph/edit', trigger_by_action='browse_interactive', error=False, observation='browse', goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:8929/admin/projects/root/janusgraph/edit'], active_page_index=0, last_browser_action=\"# Open janusgraph edit page\\nclick('678')\\nnoop(800)\", last_browser_action_error='', focused_element_bid='65'), BrowseInteractiveAction(browser_actions=\"goto('http://the-agent-company.com:8929/admin/application_settings/ci_cd')\\nnoop(800)\", thought='', browsergym_send_msg_to_user='', action='browse_interactive', security_risk=None), BrowserOutputObservation(content=\"Skip to main content \\n\\n##  Primary navigation \\n\\n[ Homepage  ](/)\\n\\nCreate new... \\n\\n  *     * [ New project/repository  ](/projects/new)\\n    * [ New group  ](/groups/new)\\n    * [ New snippet  ](/-/snippets/new)\\n\\n\\n\\nAdministrator user\u2019s menu \\n\\n  *     * [ Administrator  @root  ](/root)\\n  *     * Set status \\n    * [ Edit profile  ](/-/user_settings/profile)\\n    * [ Preferences  ](/-/profile/preferences)\\n  *     * [ Sign out  ](/users/sign_out)\\n\\n\\n\\n[ 84  ](/dashboard/issues?assignee_username=root)\\n\\n99+ \\n\\n  * Merge requests \\n\\n    * [ Assigned  7  ](/dashboard/merge_requests?assignee_username=root)\\n    * [ Review requests  157  ](/dashboard/merge_requests?reviewer_username=root)\\n\\n\\n\\n[ ](/dashboard/todos)\\n\\nSearch or go to\u2026 \\n\\nAdmin area \\n\\n  * Overview \\n\\n    * [ Dashboard  ](/admin)\\n    * [ Projects  ](/admin/projects)\\n    * [ Users  ](/admin/users)\\n    * [ Groups  ](/admin/groups)\\n    * [ Topics  ](/admin/topics)\\n    * [ Gitaly servers  ](/admin/gitaly_servers)\\n\\n  * CI/CD \\n\\n    * [ Runners  ](/admin/runners)\\n    * [ Jobs  ](/admin/jobs)\\n\\n  * Analytics \\n\\n    * [ DevOps Reports  ](/admin/dev_ops_reports)\\n    * [ Usage trends  ](/admin/usage_trends)\\n\\n  * Monitoring \\n\\n    * [ System information  ](/admin/system_info)\\n    * [ Background migrations  ](/admin/background_migrations)\\n    * [ Background jobs  ](/admin/background_jobs)\\n    * [ Health check  ](/admin/health_check)\\n\\n  * [ Messages  ](/admin/broadcast_messages)\\n  * [ System hooks  ](/admin/hooks)\\n  * [ Applications  ](/admin/applications)\\n  * [ Abuse reports  0  ](/admin/abuse_reports)\\n  * [ Deploy keys  ](/admin/deploy_keys)\\n  * [ Labels  ](/admin/labels)\\n  * * * *\\n\\nSettings \\n\\n    * [ General  ](/admin/application_settings/general)\\n    * [ Integrations  ](/admin/application_settings/integrations)\\n    * [ Repository  ](/admin/application_settings/repository)\\n    * [ CI/CD  ](/admin/application_settings/ci_cd)\\n    * [ Reporting  ](/admin/application_settings/reporting)\\n    * [ Metrics and profiling  ](/admin/application_settings/metrics_and_profiling)\\n    * [ Network  ](/admin/application_settings/network)\\n    * [ Appearance  ](/admin/application_settings/appearance)\\n    * [ Preferences  ](/admin/application_settings/preferences)\\n\\n\\n\\n\\nHelp \\n\\n  *     * [ Help  ](/help)\\n    * [ Support  ](https://about.gitlab.com/get-help/)\\n    * [ GitLab documentation  ](/help/docs)\\n    * [ Compare GitLab plans  ](https://about.gitlab.com/pricing)\\n    * [ Community forum  ](https://forum.gitlab.com)\\n    * [ Contribute to GitLab  ](/help#contribute-to-gitlab)\\n    * [ Provide feedback  ](https://about.gitlab.com/submit-feedback)\\n  *     * Keyboard shortcuts ` ? `\\n    * What's new  4 \\n\\n\\n\\n[ Admin  ](http://the-agent-company.com:8929/admin)\\n\\n[ Milestones ](/dashboard/milestones) [ Snippets ](/dashboard/snippets) [ Activity ](/dashboard/activity) [ Groups ](/dashboard/groups) [ Projects ](/dashboard/projects)\\n\\n<::before>\\n\\n##  Check your sign-up restrictions \\n\\nYour GitLab instance allows anyone to register for an account, which is a security risk on public-facing GitLab instances. You should deactivate new sign ups if public users aren't expected to register for an account. \\n\\n[ Deactivate  ](/admin/application_settings/general#js-signup-settings) Acknowledge \\n\\n<::before>\\n\\n##  OpenSSL version 3 \\n\\nStarting with GitLab 17.7, OpenSSL 3 will be used. All TLS connections require TLS 1.2 or higher. Weaker ciphers are no longer supported. Encryption must have at least of 112 bits of security. [ Learn more ](https://docs.gitlab.com/ee/update/versions/gitlab_17_changes.html#1770) . \\n\\nAcknowledge \\n\\n<::before>\\n\\nTo help improve GitLab, we would like to periodically [ collect usage information ](/help/administration/settings/usage_statistics.md) . This can be changed at any time in [ your settings ](/admin/application_settings/metrics_and_profiling#js-usage-settings) . \\n\\n[ Send service data  ](/admin/application_settings?application_setting%5Busage_ping_enabled%5D=1&application_setting%5Bversion_check_enabled%5D=1) [ Don't send service data  ](/admin/application_settings?application_setting%5Busage_ping_enabled%5D=0&application_setting%5Bversion_check_enabled%5D=0)\\n\\n  1. <::after> [ Admin area  ](/admin)\\n  2. [ CI/CD  ](/admin/application_settings/ci_cd)\\n\\n\\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Variables \\n\\nVariables store information that you can use in job scripts. All projects on the instance can use these variables. [ Learn more. ](/help/ci/variables/index.md#for-an-instance)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\nVariables can be accidentally exposed in a job log, or maliciously sent to a third party server. The masked variable feature can help reduce the risk of accidentally exposing variable values, but is not a guaranteed method to prevent malicious users from accessing variables. [ How can I make my variables more secure? ](/help/ci/variables/index.md#cicd-variable-security)\\n\\nVariables can have several attributes. [ Learn more. ](/help/ci/variables/index.md#define-a-cicd-variable-in-the-ui)\\n\\n  * <::marker> ` Protected: ` Only exposed to protected branches or protected tags. \\n  * <::marker> ` Masked: ` Hidden in job logs. Must match masking requirements. \\n  * <::marker> ` Expanded: ` Variables with ` $ ` will be treated as the start of a reference to another variable. \\n\\n\\n\\nEnvironment variables on this GitLab instance are configured to be [ protected ](/help/ci/variables/index.md?rel=noopener+noreferrer&target=_blank#protect-a-cicd-variable) by default. \\n\\n##  CI/CD Variables  0 \\n\\nAdd variable \\n\\nKey  \u2191  (Click to sort descending)  |  Value  |  Environments  |  Actions   \\n---|---|---|---  \\nThere are no variables yet.   \\n  \\nExpand \\n\\n##  Continuous Integration and Deployment \\n\\nCustomize CI/CD settings, including Auto DevOps, instance runners, and job artifacts. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n<::before><::after> Default to Auto DevOps pipeline for all projects \\n\\nThe Auto DevOps pipeline runs by default in all projects with no CI/CD configuration file. [ What is Auto DevOps? ](/help/topics/autodevops/index.md)\\n\\nAuto DevOps domain \\n\\nThe default domain to use for Auto Review Apps and Auto Deploy stages in all projects. [ Learn more. ](/help/topics/autodevops/stages.md#auto-review-apps)\\n\\n<::before><::after> Enable instance runners for new projects \\n\\nAll new projects can use instance runners by default. \\n\\nInstance runners details \\n\\nAdd a custom message with details about instance runners. The message is visible when you view runners for projects and groups. Markdown is supported. \\n\\nMaximum artifacts size (MB) \\n\\nThe maximum file size for job artifacts. [ Learn more. ](/help/administration/settings/continuous_integration.md#maximum-artifacts-size)\\n\\nMaximum artifacts archive size (bytes) \\n\\nThe maximum file size for job artifacts archive. \\n\\nDefault artifacts expiration \\n\\nSet the default expiration time for job artifacts in all projects. Set to ` 0 ` to never expire artifacts by default. If no unit is written, it defaults to seconds. For example, these are all equivalent: ` 3600 ` , ` 60 minutes ` , or ` one hour ` . [ Learn more. ](/help/administration/settings/continuous_integration.md#default-artifacts-expiration)\\n\\n<::before><::after> Keep the latest artifacts for all jobs in the latest successful pipelines \\n\\nThe latest artifacts for all jobs in the most recent successful pipelines in each project are stored and do not expire. \\n\\nArchive jobs \\n\\nJobs older than the configured time are considered expired and are archived. Archived jobs can no longer be retried. Leave empty to never archive jobs automatically. The default unit is in days, but you can use other units, for example ` 15 days ` , ` 1 month ` , ` 2 years ` . Minimum value is 1 day. [ Learn more. ](/help/administration/settings/continuous_integration.md#archive-jobs)\\n\\n<::before><::after> Protect CI/CD variables by default \\n\\nNew CI/CD variables in projects and groups default to protected. \\n\\nMaximum includes \\n\\nThe maximum number of included files per pipeline. \\n\\nMaximum downstream pipeline trigger rate \\n\\nThe maximum number of downstream pipelines that can be triggered per minute (for a given project, user, and commit). \\n\\nDefault CI/CD configuration file \\n\\nThe default CI/CD configuration file and path for new projects. [ ](/help/ci/pipelines/settings.md#specify-a-custom-cicd-configuration-file)\\n\\n<::before><::after> Enable pipeline suggestion banner \\n\\nDisplay a banner on merge requests in projects with no pipelines to initiate steps to add a .gitlab-ci.yml file. \\n\\nInstance runners expiration \\n\\nSet the expiration time of authentication tokens of newly registered instance runners. Authentication tokens are automatically reset at these intervals. If no unit is written, it defaults to seconds. For example, these are all equivalent: ` 86400 ` , ` 24 hours ` , or ` 1 day ` . Minimum value is two hours. [ Learn more. ](/help/ci/runners/configure_runners#authentication-token-security)\\n\\nGroup runners expiration \\n\\nSet the expiration time of authentication tokens of newly registered group runners. If no unit is written, it defaults to seconds. For example, these are all equivalent: ` 86400 ` , ` 24 hours ` , or ` 1 day ` . Minimum value is two hours. [ Learn more. ](/help/ci/runners/configure_runners#authentication-token-security)\\n\\nProject runners expiration \\n\\nSet the expiration time of authentication tokens of newly registered project runners. If no unit is written, it defaults to seconds. For example, these are all equivalent: ` 86400 ` , ` 24 hours ` , or ` 1 day ` . Minimum value is two hours. [ Learn more. ](/help/ci/runners/configure_runners#authentication-token-security)\\n\\n<::before><::after> Enable the external redirect warning page for job artifacts \\n\\nShow a redirect page that warns you about user-generated content in GitLab Pages. \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\n####  CI/CD limits \\n\\nBy default, set a limit to 0 to have no limit. \\n\\nMaximum number of Instance-level CI/CD variables that can be defined \\n\\nMaximum size of a dotenv artifact in bytes \\n\\nMaximum number of variables in a dotenv artifact \\n\\nMaximum number of jobs in a single pipeline \\n\\nTotal number of jobs in currently active pipelines \\n\\nMaximum number of pipeline subscriptions to and from a project \\n\\nMaximum number of pipeline schedules \\n\\nMaximum number of needs dependencies that a job can have \\n\\nThis limit cannot be disabled. Set to 0 to block all job (needs) dependencies. \\n\\nMaximum number of runners registered per group \\n\\nMaximum number of runners registered per project \\n\\nMaximum number of downstream pipelines in a pipeline's hierarchy tree \\n\\nSave Default limits \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Package Registry \\n\\nConfigure package forwarding and package file size limits. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n#####  Skip metadata URL validation for the NuGet package \\n\\nBy default, the NuGet package validates the ` projectUrl ` , ` iconUrl ` , and ` licenseUrl ` metadata. In an offline environment, you cannot upload the NuGet package with this validation because these URLs cannot be resolved. You might want to select the checkbox to skip validation. \\n\\nValidate these URLs manually to ensure malicious packages are not uploaded to the NuGet package registry. Selecting and clearing the checkbox might lead to invalid records in the package registry that you cannot update. \\n\\n<::before><::after> Skip metadata URL validation for the NuGet package \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\n####  Package file size limits \\n\\nSet limit to 0 to allow any file size. \\n\\nMaximum Conan package file size in bytes \\n\\nMaximum Helm chart file size in bytes \\n\\nMaximum Maven package file size in bytes \\n\\nMaximum npm package file size in bytes \\n\\nMaximum NuGet package file size in bytes \\n\\nMaximum PyPI package file size in bytes \\n\\nMaximum Terraform Module package file size in bytes \\n\\nGeneric package file size in bytes \\n\\nSave Default size limits \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Runners \\n\\nConfigure runner version management and registration settings. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n#####  Runner version management \\n\\n<::before><::after> Fetch GitLab Runner release version data from GitLab.com \\n\\nOfficial runner version data is periodically fetched from GitLab.com to determine whether the runners need upgrades. [ Learn more. ](/help/ci/runners/runners_scope.md#determine-which-runners-need-to-be-upgraded)\\n\\n#####  Runner registration \\n\\n<::before><::after> Allow runner registration token \\n\\nWhen disabled, runner registration tokens are disabled from runner pages, and maintainers and owners cannot use registration tokens to register runners. They can use runner authentication tokens instead as the more secure runner registration method. \\n\\n<::before><::after> Members of the project can create runners \\n\\n<::before><::after> Members of the group can create runners \\n\\nSave changes \\n\", url='http://the-agent-company.com:8929/admin/application_settings/ci_cd', trigger_by_action='browse_interactive', error=False, observation='browse', goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:8929/admin/application_settings/ci_cd'], active_page_index=0, last_browser_action=\"goto('http://the-agent-company.com:8929/admin/application_settings/ci_cd')\\nnoop(800)\", last_browser_action_error='', focused_element_bid='70'), BrowseInteractiveAction(browser_actions=\"goto('http://the-agent-company.com:8929/admin/projects')\\nnoop(500)\", thought='', browsergym_send_msg_to_user='', action='browse_interactive', security_risk=None), BrowserOutputObservation(content=\"Skip to main content \\n\\n##  Primary navigation \\n\\n[ Homepage  ](/)\\n\\nCreate new... \\n\\n  *     * [ New project/repository  ](/projects/new)\\n    * [ New group  ](/groups/new)\\n    * [ New snippet  ](/-/snippets/new)\\n\\n\\n\\nAdministrator user\u2019s menu \\n\\n  *     * [ Administrator  @root  ](/root)\\n  *     * Set status \\n    * [ Edit profile  ](/-/user_settings/profile)\\n    * [ Preferences  ](/-/profile/preferences)\\n  *     * [ Sign out  ](/users/sign_out)\\n\\n\\n\\n[ 84  ](/dashboard/issues?assignee_username=root)\\n\\n99+ \\n\\n  * Merge requests \\n\\n    * [ Assigned  7  ](/dashboard/merge_requests?assignee_username=root)\\n    * [ Review requests  157  ](/dashboard/merge_requests?reviewer_username=root)\\n\\n\\n\\n[ ](/dashboard/todos)\\n\\nSearch or go to\u2026 \\n\\nAdmin area \\n\\n  * Overview \\n\\n    * [ Dashboard  ](/admin)\\n    * [ Projects  ](/admin/projects)\\n    * [ Users  ](/