acters \\n\\nHighlight the usage of hidden unicode characters. These have innocent uses for right-to-left languages, but can also be used in potential exploits. \\n\\nCI/CD Catalog project \\n\\nSet component project as a CI/CD Catalog project. [ What is the CI/CD Catalog? ](/help/ci/components/index#cicd-catalog)\\n\\nCI/CD Catalog project \\n\\nThe project will be findable in the CI/CD Catalog after the project has at least one release. \\n\\nSave changes \\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Badges \\n\\nAdd badges to display information about this project. [ What are badges? ](/help/user/project/badges.md)\\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n##  Your badges  0 \\n\\nAdd new badge \\n\\nName  |  Badge  |  URL  |  Actions   \\n---|---|---|---  \\nThis project has no badges. Start by adding a new badge.   \\n  \\nExpand \\n\\n##  Service Desk \\n\\nEnable and disable Service Desk. Some additional configuration might be required. [ Learn more ](/help/user/project/service_desk/index.md) . \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n##  Improve customer support with Service Desk \\n\\nService Desk allows people to create issues in your GitLab instance without their own user account. It provides a unique email address for end users to create issues in a project. Replies can be sent either through the GitLab interface or by email. End users only see threads through email. \\n\\n[ Configure Service Desk  ](/help/user/project/service_desk/configure.md)\\n\\nExpand \\n\\n##  Advanced \\n\\nHousekeeping, export, archive, change path, transfer, and delete. \\n\\n<::before><::after>\\n\\n####  Housekeeping \\n\\nRuns a number of housekeeping tasks within the current repository, such as compressing file revisions and removing unreachable objects. [ Learn more. ](/help/administration/housekeeping.md)\\n\\n[ Run housekeeping  ](/root/bustub/housekeeping) Prune unreachable objects \\n\\n####  Export project \\n\\nExport this project with all its related data in order to move it to a new GitLab instance. When the exported file is ready, you can download it from this page or from the download link in the email notification you will receive. You can then import it when creating a new project. [ Learn more. ](/help/user/project/settings/import_export.md)\\n\\nThe following items will be exported: \\n\\n  * <::marker>Project and wiki repositories \\n  * <::marker>Project uploads \\n  * <::marker>Project configuration, excluding integrations \\n  * <::marker>Issues with comments, merge requests with diffs and comments, labels, milestones, snippets, and other project entities \\n  * <::marker>LFS objects \\n  * <::marker>Issue Boards \\n  * <::marker>Design Management files and data \\n\\n\\n\\nThe following items will NOT be exported: \\n\\n  * <::marker>Job logs and artifacts \\n  * <::marker>Container registry images \\n  * <::marker>CI variables \\n  * <::marker>Pipeline triggers \\n  * <::marker>Webhooks \\n  * <::marker>Any encrypted tokens \\n\\n\\n\\n[ Export project  ](/root/bustub/export)\\n\\n####  Archive project \\n\\nArchiving the project makes it entirely read-only. It is hidden from the dashboard and doesn't display in searches. **The repository cannot be committed to, and no issues, comments, or other entities can be created.** [ Learn more. ](/help/user/project/working_with_projects.md#archive-a-project)\\n\\n[ Archive project  ](/root/bustub/archive)\\n\\n####  Change path \\n\\nA project\u2019s repository name defines its URL (the one you use to access the project via a browser) and its place on the file disk where GitLab is installed. [ Learn more. ](/help/user/project/working_with_projects.md#rename-a-repository)\\n\\n  * <::marker>Be careful. Renaming a project's repository can have unintended side effects. \\n  * <::marker>You will need to update your local repositories to point to the new location. \\n\\nPath \\n\\nhttp://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/ \\n\\nChange path \\n\\n####  Transfer project \\n\\nTransfer your project into another namespace. [ Learn more. ](/help/user/project/settings/migrate_projects.md#transfer-a-project-to-another-namespace)\\n\\nA project\u2019s repository name defines its URL (the one you use to access the project via a browser) and its place on the file disk where GitLab is installed. [ Learn more. ](/help/user/project/working_with_projects.md#rename-a-repository)\\n\\nWhen you transfer your project to a group, you can easily manage multiple projects, view usage quotas for storage, compute minutes, and users, and start a trial or upgrade to a paid tier. \\n\\nDon't have a group? [ Create one ](/groups/new)\\n\\nThings to be aware of before transferring: \\n\\n  * <::marker>Be careful. Changing the project's namespace can have unintended side effects. \\n  * <::marker>You can only transfer the project to namespaces you manage. \\n  * <::marker>You will need to update your local repositories to point to the new location. \\n  * <::marker>Project visibility level will be changed to match namespace rules when transferring to a group. \\n\\n\\n\\nSelect a new namespace \\n\\nSelect a new namespace \\n\\n  * No results found. \\n\\n\\n\\n\\nTransfer project \\n\\n####  Delete project \\n\\n**Deleting the project will delete its repository and all related resources, including issues and merge requests.**\\n\\n**Deleted projects cannot be restored!**\\n\\nDelete project \\n\\n##  Loading  Saving project. \\n\\nPlease wait a moment, this page will automatically refresh when ready. \\n\", url='http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/bustub/edit', trigger_by_action='browse_interactive', error=True, observation='browse', goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/bustub/edit'], active_page_index=0, last_browser_action=\"goto('http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/bustub/edit')\\nnoop(800)\\n# Scroll to bottom and click 'Delete project'\\nscroll(0, 2000)\\nnoop(400)\\nclick('a11')\\nnoop(500)\\n# Confirm by typing project path and clicking confirm\\nfill('a23', 'r